<section id="what-i-offer">
  <h2>Why Mentoring?</h2>

    <p>
      It feels good to have ten thousand ideas. You only make progress on the ones you work on until they're done.
    </p>

    <p>
      You've got a project list, writing a Kubernetes operator, learning Terraform, getting to grips with shell scripting, developing build pipelines. You know that the materials are all free and online, and somehow that makes it worse because there's nothing stopping you except you.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can ask a model for guidance, but the next thing you know you're researching a thousand projects instead of working on your goal.
    </p>
    <p>
      Michael, an engineer I worked with, was honest with me: he needed someone pointing him back to his goals every two weeks, until he learned the habit of managing daily distractions against his long term goals. 
    </p>
    <p>
      That's what I do. You tell me what you're building, what you want to learn, in a free session. We write it down. We meet up and make progress regularly.</p>
      <p> 
      As you're learning to stay on track, you've also got a friendly, experienced infrastructure and software engineer available to you, helping you make progress, until you're confident you've mastered your goals.
    </p>
  </section>
